      "title": "TRANSFER AND ACADEMIC SERVICES SPECIALIST",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\n\nLocation: Rochester Hills\n\nJOB TITLE:   Transfer and Academic Services Specialist  DEPARTMENT: Office of the Registrar  REPORTS TO:  Registrar COLLEGE MISSION:   Rochester Christian University is a Christ-centered institution that empowers students to lead lives of personal and professional significance while serving God in a changing world. POSITION SUMMARY:  The Transfer Credit Specialist serves as a pivotal link in facilitating seamless credit evaluation and transfer processes for students transferring between institutions or academic programs at Rochester Christian University. This role involves comprehensive assessment of transcripts, articulation agreements, and collaboration with various stakeholders to ensure accurate credit recognition and a smooth transition for students. This person also serves as our academic Accommodations Officer, Testing Center Coordinator, and Rize administrator.  EDUCATION AND/OR EXPERIENCE REQUIRED:   A minimum of an Associate’s degree from an accredited college or university; a baccalaureate degree preferred  Preferred experience working in higher education settings  Preferred experience in articulation agreements and transfer credit evaluation  Preferred experience with TES/Transferology  Preferred experience with accommodations  An equivalent combination of related work and education experience  ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:   Maintain the articulation repository and web page  Maintain transfer equivalency database  Mi Transfer Liaison  Syllabi collection and review  MACRAO Representative for the Michigan Transfer Network  Manage the creation and maintenance of articulation agreements and transfer guides with partner schools  Manage Rize Platform, including setup, registration, grades, attendance, etc.  Stay informed of current state and federal regulations regarding student records.  Utilizes RCU’s evaluation system and other resources to complete transfer evaluations for prospective and current students  Responsible for providing exceptional customer service to support RCU’s incoming transfer student population, administrators, faculty, and staff.  Maintains current knowledge of all academic changes to RCU degree programs.  Process academic accommodations requests from students  Send out regular communication regarding academic accommodations to students and faculty  Schedule and proctor tests in the testing center for students with accommodations  Other duties as assigned in accordance with departmental needs. REQUIRED SKILLS AND ABILITIES:   Experience working with CAMS Enterprise or a similar student management system  Highly dedicated to service excellence for students, faculty, and staff  Ability to work independently and collaboratively with University constituents.  Exceptional problem-solving, administrative, analytical, interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills.  Working knowledge of the Microsoft Office Suite and Google Drive documents.  The ability to prioritize work effectively and manage time efficiently.  An understanding of institutional structure in an educational environment.  Flexibility to learn new methodologies, technologies, and systems.  Ability to network with members of Rochester Christian University and outside partners  Ability to collaborate effectively with campus departments, faculty, parents, and students    Supportive of the University's mission. Indicators of this support include a demonstrated personal faith in Jesus Christ and being active in a local church.",
